<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Totonacs</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Totonacs are an indigenous people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-coast-of-mexico">Gulf Coast of Mexico</a>, centred on the region of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veracruz">Veracruz</a>, whose city of Cempoala was subject to Aztec tribute. When the Spanish landed in 1519 the Totonacs allied with them against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a> profile lists the Totonacs among the subject peoples who joined the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> to destroy the power that had extracted tribute from them.</p></div>
